$ HELP
commands (115200 8N1):
  HELP                  this list
  INFO                  fw / module baud / counters
  LIST                  stored codes: id band code
  LIST LONG             id band code name group sym flags
  SEND <id>             transmit once (frame dur=03)
  LONG <id>             start continuous transmit (dur=FE)
  STOP <id>             stop continuous transmit (dur=FF)
  ERASE <id|all>        delete one code / all codes (ids shift)
  DEDUP                 merge records with same band+addr+button (osc differs)
  NEW <band> <hex> [name]  add a manual code (315/433, 8 hex)
  NAME <id> [text]      set/clear UTF-8 name (max 24 bytes)
  SYM <id> [text]       set/clear symbol (max 8 bytes)
  GROUP <id> [text]     set/clear single group (max 16 bytes)
  EDIT <id> band|code <v>  edit raw band / 4-byte payload
  MODE single|continuous  module decode output mode
  BAUD <n>              module baud 4800/9600/57600/115200
  RECOVER               scan module baud and force it back to 9600
  RAW <hex>             send raw bytes to module (debug)
  MON ON|OFF            hex-dump every module byte (debug)
  ECHO ON|OFF           print decoded frames (default ON)
  DISP ON|OFF|TEST [s]|SHOW  OLED panel / test pattern / ASCII dump
  WIFI [status]|[ssid pass]|CLEAR  join an AP / forget STA (AP fallback)
  BLE [on|off]          BLE advertising / status
  PIN                   show BLE 4-digit PIN (serial only)
  OTA | OTA OFF         arm firmware upload (token on serial/OLED, 10 min)
  STATE                 print JSON state snapshot
  WEBTEST               self-check HTTP /api/hello + /api/events
  RESET                 restart ESP32

code = addr2 addr1 button osc (8 hex); osc 0x30..0xF0 (default 0x60)
identity = band + addr2 + addr1 + button; osc is NOT part of identity

learn: press a remote button; firmware prints LEARN id=... automatically
note: SEND gets F0 after ~0.85s; LONG gets 0xFE heartbeat; STOP gets 0xFF (measured)

